.TH GHLOG2DT 1 2026-10-27 "ghlog2dt" "User Commands"
.nh
.SH NAME
ghlog2dt \- ship GitHub Actions job logs to Dynatrace
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ghlog2dt run
.RB [ \-\-repo
.IR owner/name ]...
.RB [ \-\-all ]
.RB [ \-\-run\-id
.IR id
.RB [ \-\-run\-attempt
.IR n ]]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RI [ flags ]
.br
.B ghlog2dt list
.RI [ flags ]
.br
.B ghlog2dt fetch
.RI [ flags ]
.RI < jobs.ndjson
.br
.B ghlog2dt ship
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RI < records.ndjson
.br
.B ghlog2dt checkpoint
.BR show | merge | prune | mark | rewind
.I ...
.br
.B ghlog2dt token
.B \-\-app\-id
.I id
.RB [ \-\-permission
.IR name=level ]...
.br
.B ghlog2dt schedule
.RB [ \-\-interval
.IR minutes ]
.RB [ \-\-offset
.IR minutes ]
.RB [ \-\-rewrite
.IR workflow.yml ]
.br
.B ghlog2dt version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I ghlog2dt
reads the logs of completed GitHub Actions jobs through the REST API and
posts them, one JSON record per line, to the Dynatrace Log Monitoring API v2
.RB ( "POST /api/v2/logs/ingest" ).
It keeps one checkpoint file per repository so that each job is shipped
once, waits for unfinished runs, and drops lines older than
.B max_age
because Dynatrace refuses logs older than 24 hours.
.PP
.B run
is the production path: for each target repository it lists runs created
since the high\-water mark minus
.BR \-\-lookback ,
re\-polls pending runs, downloads and parses new job logs, batches and posts
the records, and saves the checkpoint.
With
.B \-\-run\-id
it ships one run (event mode) and leaves the high\-water mark alone.
.PP
.BR list ,
.B fetch
and
.B ship
are the same stages as filters over newline\-delimited JSON:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ghlog2dt list \-\-repo CoolGitOrg/app\-a | ghlog2dt fetch | ghlog2dt ship
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B list
never writes the checkpoint; the pipeline is for inspection and repair.
.PP
.B checkpoint
inspects and edits checkpoints:
.B show
prints one,
.B merge
combines files (latest high\-water mark, union of pending runs and shipped
jobs),
.B prune
expires old entries,
.B mark
records job IDs as shipped,
.B rewind \-\-to
.I 6h
lowers the high\-water mark, and with
.B \-\-forget
also forgets jobs shipped since then so they are sent again.
.PP
.B token
mints a GitHub App installation token: an RS256 JWT, an installation
lookup, and a POST to access_tokens.
.PP
.B schedule
prints the cron expression and lookback for an export interval (5, 6, 10,
12, 15, 20, 30 or 60 minutes) and can rewrite the line tagged
.B "# ghlog2dt:cron"
in a workflow file.
.SH OPTIONS
Options common to most commands:
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
JSON configuration file (default
.IR ghlog2dt.json ;
an explicitly named file must exist).
.TP
.BI \-\-repo " owner/name"
Target repository; repeatable or comma separated.
.TP
.B \-\-all
Every repository the installation token can see, filtered by
.B \-\-include
and
.B \-\-exclude
globs.
.TP
.BI \-\-workflow " glob"
Only runs whose workflow name or path matches.
.TP
.BI \-\-lookback " duration"
Overlap window behind the high\-water mark (default 90m).
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-age " duration"
Oldest line or window ever considered (default 23h45m, at most 24h).
.TP
.BI \-\-stale " drop|rewrite"
What to do with lines older than max\-age.
.TP
.BI \-\-state " dir"
Checkpoint directory (default
.IR state ).
.TP
.BI \-\-dt\-url " url"
Dynatrace environment, e.g.
.IR https://abc12345.live.dynatrace.com .
.TP
.BI \-\-dt\-auth " Api\-Token|Bearer"
Authorization scheme.
.TP
.BI \-\-batch\-bytes " n" "\fR, \fP\-\-batch\-records " n
Request limits (defaults 4 MiB and 5000; Dynatrace allows 10 MB and 50000).
.TP
.B \-\-gzip
Compress request bodies (not documented by Dynatrace; verify first).
.TP
.B \-\-header\-attrs
Send job\-level attributes once per request in X\-Dynatrace\-Attr.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Write records as NDJSON instead of posting; never save the checkpoint.
.TP
.BI \-\-summary " file"
Where the JSON summary goes (default stdout).
.TP
.B \-\-print\-config
Print the effective configuration with secrets elided.
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-format " json|text" "\fR, \fP\-\-log\-level " level
Diagnostics on standard error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GH_TOKEN
GitHub token with Actions read access (fallback
.BR GITHUB_TOKEN ).
.TP
.B DT_LOGS_TOKEN
Dynatrace token with the
.B logs.ingest
scope.
.TP
.BR DT_URL ", " DT_AUTH_SCHEME
Ingest endpoint and scheme.
.TP
.BR GHLOG_CONFIG ", " GHLOG_TARGET_REPOS ", " GHLOG_LOOKBACK ", " GHLOG_STATE_DIR ", " GHLOG_CONCURRENCY ", " GHLOG_GZIP
Overrides for the corresponding configuration keys.
.TP
.B GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY
If set, a Markdown summary is appended to it.
.PP
Secrets are accepted only from the environment.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I state/owner__name.json
Checkpoint for one repository: high_water, pending_runs, shipped_jobs.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success.
.TP
1
A repository failed.
.TP
2
Usage or configuration error.
.TP
3
Partial success: Dynatrace refused some records or they were too old.
.TP
4
Authentication failed (GitHub or Dynatrace).
.TP
5
GitHub rate limit too far from reset, or Dynatrace budget exhausted (402).
.TP
6
Checkpoint could not be read or written.
.SH EXAMPLES
Show what would be shipped for one repository:
.PP
.RS
.nf
GH_TOKEN=$(ghlog2dt token \-\-app\-id 123456 \-\-key\-file app.pem \e
    \-\-permission actions=read)
ghlog2dt run \-\-repo CoolGitOrg/app\-a \-\-dry\-run | jq \-c '{severity, content}'
.fi
.RE
.PP
Export every 10 minutes:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ghlog2dt schedule \-\-interval 10 \-\-rewrite .github/workflows/forward.yml
.fi
.RE
.PP
Replay the last six hours of one repository:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ghlog2dt checkpoint rewind \-\-repo CoolGitOrg/app\-a \-\-to 6h \-\-forget
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gh (1),
.BR jq (1)
.PP
Dynatrace Log Monitoring API v2; GitHub REST API "Workflow runs" and
"Workflow jobs".
.SH BUGS
Pull mode finds runs by creation time, so a re-run of a run created before
the window is not seen; use the event (push) mode for that.
